\pard\tx2380\b0\fs28\fi-1960\li2380\fc0\cf0 DESCRIPTION	
\b snddriver_dsp_boot()
\b0  enqueues a command to boot the DSP.  The arguments are as follows:\

\fs20 \

\pard\tx2760\tx3140\tx3520\fs28\fi-380\li2760\fc0\cf0 ·	
\i commandPort
\i0  is the DSP command port, as retrieved by 
\b snddriver_get_dsp_cmd_port()
\b0 .  \

\fs20 \

\fs28 ·	
\i bootImage
\i0  is a pointer to a DSP program image that's downloaded to the DSP (program memory location 0x0) and immediately executed.  The image is created by reading a ª.lodº file that's assembled from DSP56001 assembly code.\

\fs20 \

\fs28 ·	
\i imageSize
\i0  is the size of the DSP boot image, in bytes.  The image must not exceed 512 words (24-bit DSP words right-justified within 32-bit integers).\

\fs20 \

\fs28 ·	
\i priority
\i0  is one of the three priority constants SNDDRIVER_LOW_PRIORITY, SNDDRIVER_MED_PRIORITY, or SNDDRIVER_HIGH_PRIORITY.  The sound driver sorts the commands in its DSP command queue according to priority.\

\fs20 \

\fs28\fi0\li2380 Booting the DSP clears neither external memory nor on-chip data memory.\

\fs20 \

\b\fs28 snddriver_dsp_reset()
\b0  puts the DSP in its reset state.  By this it's meant that the DSP's execution is immediately halted and a bootstrap program is awaited.  Booting the DSP automatically resets it, thus you don't need to call this function before calling 
\b snddriver_boot_dsp()
\b0 .  \

\fs20 \

\fs10 \

\pard\tx2380\fs28\fi-1320\li2380\fc0\cf0 RETURN	Returns an error code:  0 on success, nonzero on failure.\

