\pard\tx2380\b0\fs28\fi-1960\li2380\fc0\cf0 DESCRIPTION	These functions let you control the number and size of the DMA buffers that are used to transfer data in a stream.\

\fs20 \

\pard\tx2760\tx3140\tx3520\b\fs28\li2380\fc0\cf0 snddriver_set_sndout_bufcount()
\b0  sets the number of buffers that are used when playing back sounds; the 
\i count
\i0  argument, which must be greater than 0, establishes the buffer count.  Four buffers are used in the default configuration.  \

\fs20 \

\b\fs28 snddriver_set_sndout_bufsize()
\b0  sets the size of the sound-out buffers (in bytes) to the value of the 
\i size
\i0  argument.  This function is needed only if you're using a linked stream to sound-out (see the 
\b snddriver_stream_setup()
\b0  function for more on linked streams).  The value of 
\i size
\i0  must be no greater than 
\b vm_page_size
\b0 , the size of a page of virtual memory; the default is 
\b vm_page_size
\b0 .  If you're writing directly to the sound-out streamÐin other words if the stream to sound-out is configured as SNDDRIVER_STREAM_TO_SNDOUT_22 or ...SNDOUT_44Ðthe size of the sound-out buffers is computed from the 
\i sampleCount
\i0  argument to 
\b snddriver_stream_setup()
\b0  and the size set here is ignored.\

\fs20 \

\fs28 For both of these functions, the 
\i devicePort
\i0  and 
\i sndoutPort
\i0  arguments are ports to the sound driver device and to sound-out, as acquired through 
\b SNDAcquire()
\b0 .\

\fs20 \

\b\fs28 snddriver_stream_ndma()
\b0  sets, to 
\i count
\i0 , the number of DMA transfer buffers that are used to receive data from sound-in, and to transmit and receive data to and from the DSP.  The DMA buffer count can be set on a region-by-region basis; the stream and region to which a particular setting applies are identified by the 
\i streamPort
\i0  and 
\i regionTag
\i0  arguments, respectively.  Note that in a linked stream to sound-out, the buffer count to and from the DSP is automatically set to the sound-out buffer count (overruling the setting made through this function).\

\fs20 \

\fs10 \

\pard\tx2380\fs28\fi-1320\li2380\fc0\cf0 RETURN	Returns an error code:  0 on success, nonzero on failure.\

\fs20 \

